    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate leaning heavily into power-speed upside, headlined by **Mickey Moniak** (75.75) and **James Wood** (69.82). **Mickey Moniak** is our definitive top play, as he draws a highly favorable matchup against a 4.92 xERA arm, bolstered by a massive +14% platoon edge and significant park factors. Meanwhile, **James Wood** remains a must-start in the utility slot; his elite 0.424 xwOBA and top-of-the-order positioning provide an exceptionally high floor even against a neutral matchup. We are also monitoring **Tyler Soderstrom** (65.94) and **Henry Bolte** (60.09) closely; while both face the challenge of Framber Valdez, the combination of favorable park factors and high-leverage order positioning outweighs the danger of the opposing SP\u2019s skill set.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Isaac Paredes** (48.51). He narrowly missed the cut because he is slated against deGrom, whose 3.08 xERA creates too much volatility for our weekly scoring constraints, especially when compared to the efficient, high-ceiling profiles of **Austin Riley** (67.16) and **Corbin Carroll** (62.09). We are also tracking several \"Lineup Pending\" designations, most notably for **Brice Turang** and **Jose Caballero**. While **Jose Caballero** (59.97) is currently projected to start, the significant wind-in warning at his park creates a potential volatility trap that could see his score dip if he\u2019s forced to sacrifice contact quality for fly-ball distance. \n\nFinally, a note on our scarcity strategy: we continue to protect our stolen base potential despite tough matchups. **Seiya Suzuki** (55.24) and **Brice Turang** (48.49) draw challenging left-handed starters, but their roles as dynamic base runners keep them in the mix to offset the risks posed by elite arms like Fried and Suter. We are keeping **Dalton Rushing** on the bench today, as his sub-40 floor score makes him a clear violation of our efficiency protocols, preserving our remaining game caps for higher-leverage situations later in the week.",
